<!--
  RM_FeverWoodBirds.xml                       FEVERWOOD_ALIEN_BIRD_CHORUS_1

  The crown's four birds (fever_wood_fauna_roster_2026-09-23.md §5 — the
  exact defNames/labels/silhouettes/roles below are already authored, not
  invented here). Owner, verbatim: "Perhaps dramatic beautiful birds that
  swoop, shrill, and warble to create the typical 'swamp cacaphony' that
  replaces the eerie silence the webwork squares already specialize in? ...
  And these should be alien birds, not just parrots. Very strange.
  Membranous, hairy, or weirdly shaped feathers."

  | # | defName      | role                                          |
  | 1 | RM_Chellow   | tameable — a private chorus near the base     |
  | 2 | RM_Murrelith | plumage worth money (CompShearable)           |
  | 3 | RM_Thavrik   | nests worth raiding (CompProperties_EggLayer) |
  | 4 | RM_Skellick  | thief — see RimProperty's own wild-theft patch|

  🔑 The chorus/silence mechanism this item exists for is NOT a per-bird
  SoundDef — §6c/the item's own "open" section leaves how the call registers
  divide (swoop/shrill/warble) and how many birds voice it UNSET, and this
  pass does not guess it. What ships instead is the mechanism the sitting
  actually ruled: "the crown goes quiet ONLY for the water" is the Fever
  Wood's EXISTING biome ambient soundscape (map.Biome.soundsAmbient, the
  same ambient list RM_MapComponent_SilenceCue already hushes for the
  Greentide's predator-hunt cue and the mirror-break event) falling silent
  for exactly as long as RM_MapComponent_TentacleWatch's own sentinelCount
  is up — wired in RM_CompTentacleLimb.cs via the new BeginSustainedHush/
  EndSustainedHush entry points on RM_MapComponent_SilenceCue, closing the
  gap FEVER_WOOD_MECHANICS_1's F2 pass and this roster's own header both
  named ("the actual bird chorus is a separate, not-yet-built system").
  These four birds are the CAST that makes the crown loud enough for that
  silence to read as a event — living inside the wildAnimals band the
  design calls "the loudest place on the planet, deliberately" — not a
  sound-effect delivery system of their own.

  Flight: standing rule, if it flies in the fiction it flies in the game.
  All four take real Core 1.6 flight (MaxFlightTime/FlightCooldown +
  flightStartChanceOnJobStart/canFlyIntoMap/canLeaveMapFlying), same shape
  as RM_FleetFlier (TheForge, already shipped) and Core's own Chicken/
  Sparrow (MaxFlightTime/FlightCooldown statBases, verified via RimSage).
  No flyingAnimationFramePathPrefix — per the standing rule, never block
  flight waiting on frames; these fly with no wing-beat until frames exist.

  Art: this item's own step 5 (CLAUDE.md "check for existing regenerated
  art before queuing more") found all four birds already have artpipe jobs
  QUEUED for every facing (infrastructure/artpipe/pending/feverwood_
  {chellow,murrelith,thavrik,skellick}_{south,east,north}.json,
  rimflow_item_id FEVERWOOD_RM_MOD_BUILD_1) — but registry.jsonl shows every
  attempt so far recorded "fail" and _artsrc/ is empty for all twelve. This
  pass does NOT re-queue (already queued, already failing — a duplicate job
  fixes nothing) and does not chase the generator; it ships the same
  flat-colour placeholder convention this biome already uses for
  RM_Vaulm/RM_Ollareth/RM_Drommath/RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile (128x128, fully
  opaque RGBA, Graphic_Multi south/east/north — the placeholder script that
  wrote them lives at Textures/Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_FeverWoodBirds/
  make_placeholders.py in this same commit). Real bespoke art per the
  membranous/hairy/strange brief is owed to the standing art pipeline once
  the generator succeeds on these prompts.

  Commonalities are ENGINEERING DEFAULTS, not owner-set values — same
  posture as the sap-sucker guild's own wildAnimals rows.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef Name="RM_FeverWoodBirdBase" ParentName="AnimalThingBase" Abstract="true">
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>3.2</MoveSpeed>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>5</ComfyTemperatureMin>
